@startuml SABER Benchmark Framework Architecture - Current Implementation

!theme plain
title SABER Benchmark Framework - Current Implementation (Directory-Based YAML + Episode Dependencies)

skinparam class {
    BackgroundColor lightblue
    BorderColor black
    ArrowColor black
    FontSize 10
}

package "Benchmark Framework Core" {

    class BenchmarkManager {
        +domain: str
        +config_dir: Path
        +tasks_dir_path: Path
        +tasks: Dict[str, Task]
        +benchmark_config: Dict[str, Any]
        +config_loader: BenchmarkConfigLoader
        +prompt_generator: PromptGenerator
        --
        +load_tasks_from_directory(): void
        +validate_all_task_templates(): void
        +get_benchmark_info(): BenchmarkInfo
        +get_task(task_id: str): Task
        +get_subtask(task_id: str, subtask_id: str): SubTask
        +list_tasks(): List[Dict[str, Any]]
        +get_benchmark_config(): Dict[str, Any]
        +get_episode_config(task_id: str): Dict[str, Any]
        +get_task_prompt(task_id: str, prompt_type: str): str
        +render_judge_prompt_for_episode(task_id: str, episode: Episode): Any
        +get_dependency_config(): Dict[str, float]
        +_inject_judge_prompt_renderers(): void
    }

    class BenchmarkInfo {
        +domain: str
        +tasks: List[TaskInfo]
        +total_tasks: int
        +total_episodes: int
        --
        +to_dict(): Dict[str, Any]
        +get_task_by_id(task_id: str): Optional[TaskInfo]
        +get_task_ids(): List[str]
    }

    class TaskInfo {
        +task_id: str
        +title: str
        +description: str
        +episode_attempts: int
        +subtask_count: int
        +max_steps: int
        +instruction_prompt: str
        +assistant_prompt: str
        +submit_prompt: str
    }

    class BenchmarkConfigLoader {
        +domain: str
        +benchmark_config: Dict[str, Any]
        +global_defaults: Dict[str, Any]
        +permanent_environment: Optional[str]
        --
        +load_tasks_from_directory(tasks_dir_path: str): Dict[str, Task]
        +load_benchmark_config(): Dict[str, Any]
        +get_permanent_environment(): Optional[str]
        +get_dependency_config(): Dict[str, float]
        +_parse_task(task_data: Dict): Task
        +_parse_subtask(subtask_data: Dict): SubTask
        +_load_global_config(tasks_dir: Path): Dict[str, Any]
        +_apply_global_defaults(task_config: Dict): Dict
    }

    class Task {
        +task_id: str
        +domain: str
        +title: str
        +description: str
        +prompts: Dict[str, str]
        +subtasks: List[SubTask]
        +initial_context: Dict[str, Any]
        +environment: Optional[Union[str, Dict[str, Any]]]
        +allowed_executors: Optional[List[str]]
        +execution_config: Dict[str, Any]
        +episode_config: Dict[str, Any]
        +benchmark_config: Dict[str, Any]
        +evaluation_config: Dict[str, Any]
        +depends_on_task_id: Optional[str]
        +_subtask_map: Dict[str, SubTask]
        --
        +add_subtask(subtask: SubTask): void
        +get_subtask_by_id(subtask_id: str): Optional[SubTask]
        +is_complete(): bool
        +get_all_subtask_ids(): Set[str]
        +get_episode_attempts(): int
    }

    class SubTask {
        +subtask_id: str
        +task_id: str
        +title: str
        +description: str
        +objective: str
        +hint: Optional[str]
        --
        +is_dependent_on(subtask_id: str): bool
    }
}

package "Episode Management (Pydantic Models in base.py)" {

    class EpisodeManager {
        +episodes: Dict[str, Episode]
        +session_episodes: Dict[str, List[str]]
        +completed_episodes: Dict[str, Episode]
        +episode_configs: Dict[str, Dict[str, Any]]
        --
        +get_episode_by_id(episode_id: str): Optional[Episode]
        +get_session_episodes(session_id: str, include_completed: bool): List[Episode]
        +get_active_episodes_for_session(session_id: str): List[Episode]
        +add_episode_to_session(session_id: str, episode: Episode): void
        +complete_episode(episode_id: str): Optional[Episode]
        +find_available_episode_for_dependency(session_id: str, target_task_id: str, dependent_task_id: str): Optional[str]
        +find_available_episode_for_dependency_with_retry(session_id: str, target_task_id: str, dependent_task_id: str, max_wait_seconds: float, retry_interval: float, max_retry_interval: float): Optional[str]
        +attach_episode_to_episode(dependent_episode_id: str, target_episode_id: str): void
        +configure_for_task(episode_id: str, task: Task): void
        +should_terminate_episode(episode_id: str): tuple[bool, str]
        +start_episode(session_id: str, task_id: str, initial_context: Optional[Dict], task: Optional[Task]): Episode
        +step(episode_id: str, action: Action, command_result: CommandResult): StepResult
        +end_episode(episode_id: str, reason: str, result: Optional[str]): Episode
        +get_episode_state(episode_id: str): Optional[EpisodeState]
        +create_step(episode: Episode, action: Action, response: CommandResult): Step
        +update_episode_state(episode: Episode, step: Step): void
        +cleanup_session(session_id: str): void
        +remove_episode_on_error(episode_id: str, error: Exception): void
    }

    class Episode {
        +episode_id: str
        +task_id: str
        +session_id: str
        +start_time: datetime
        +end_time: Optional[datetime]
        +state: EpisodeState
        +steps: List[Step]
        +context: Dict[str, Any]
        +metadata: Dict[str, Any]
        +completion_reason: Optional[str]
        +max_steps: int
        +submission: Optional[str]
        +eval_submission: Optional[EvalSubmission]
        +depends_on_task_id: Optional[str]
        +attached_to_episode_id: Optional[str]
        +attached_episode_ids: List[str]
        --
        +add_step(step: Step): void
        +get_executed_commands(): List[str]
        +attach_to_episode(target_episode_id: str): void
        +add_attached_episode(episode_id: str): void
        +has_attached_episode_with_task(task_id: str, episodes_by_id: Dict): bool
        +is_complete: bool (property)
        +duration: Optional[float] (property)
    }

    class Step {
        +step_number: int
        +timestamp: datetime
        +action: Action
        +response: Dict[str, Any]
        +context_snapshot: Dict[str, Any]
        +done: bool
    }

    class Action {
        +tool_name: str
        +parameters: Dict[str, Any]
        +timestamp: datetime
    }

    class StepResult {
        +step: Step
        +should_terminate: bool
        +termination_reason: Optional[str]
    }

    enum EpisodeState {
        CREATED
        ACTIVE
        COMPLETED
        FAILED
        TIMEOUT
        RESET
    }
}

' Relationships
BenchmarkManager *-- BenchmarkConfigLoader
BenchmarkManager *-- Task
BenchmarkManager ..> BenchmarkInfo : creates

BenchmarkConfigLoader ..> Task : creates
BenchmarkConfigLoader ..> SubTask : creates

BenchmarkInfo *-- TaskInfo

Task *-- SubTask
Task ..> Episode : depends_on_task_id

EpisodeManager *-- Episode
Episode *-- Step
Step *-- Action
Episode ..> EpisodeState
EpisodeManager ..> StepResult : returns

note top of BenchmarkManager
**Task Definition Manager with Prompt Generation**
Loads YAML-based task definitions from directory structure.
Validates all templates at startup (fail-fast).
Supports three distinct prompt types per task:
- instruction: Initial agent instructions
- assistant: Assistant/system context
- submit: Submission guidance
Injects judge prompt renderers for llm_judge evaluation tasks.
Provides complete BenchmarkInfo for client-side orchestration.
No server-side task queue management.
end note

note top of BenchmarkInfo
**Client-Side Orchestration Data**
Pure data container for benchmark information.
Contains pre-rendered prompts for all tasks.
Clients use this to manage their own task execution order.
Replaces old server-side BenchmarkSession concept.
end note

note top of Task
**Complete Task Configuration Container**
Enhanced with:
- prompts: Dict with "instruction", "assistant", "submit" templates
- depends_on_task_id: Task-level dependency for episode attachment
- environment: Optional[Union[str, Dict]] flexible specification
- execution_config: Timeouts and execution limits
- episode_config: RL episode parameters (max_steps, timeouts)
- benchmark_config: Benchmark-level settings (episode_attempts)
- evaluation_config: Evaluation strategy and criteria
Prompts validated at startup - no runtime failures.
end note

note top of SubTask
**Simplified Informational SubTask**
Purely informational - no progression logic.
No entry/exit criteria or completion conditions.
Pydantic BaseModel for easy serialization.
Contains hint field for optional guidance.
Dependencies removed (use Task.depends_on_task_id for episode deps).
end note

note top of EpisodeManager
**RL Episode Lifecycle Manager with Dependency Support**
Manages episode creation, stepping, and completion.
Configured per episode with task-specific episode_config.
Supports episode dependencies via:
- find_available_episode_for_dependency(): Synchronous lookup
- find_available_episode_for_dependency_with_retry(): Async retry with backoff
- attach_episode_to_episode(): Link dependent episodes
Tracks both active and completed episodes.
Server no longer enforces step limits (client responsibility).
Returns StepResult with termination signals.
end note

note top of Episode
**Pydantic Episode Model with Dependency Tracking**
Pydantic BaseModel in base.py for serialization.
Complete action-response history for RL training.
Dependency tracking fields:
- depends_on_task_id: Task ID this episode needs to connect to
- attached_to_episode_id: Episode ID this is attached to
- attached_episode_ids: Episodes attached to this one
Supports eval_submission for rich evaluation data capture.
Properties for computed values (duration, is_complete).
end note

note top of BenchmarkConfigLoader
**Directory-Based YAML Parser with Global Defaults**
Loads tasks from directory structure:
- global.yaml: Domain-wide defaults and configuration
- *.yaml: Individual task files (can contain multiple tasks)
- Subdirectories supported for organization
Deep merges global defaults with task-specific configs.
Validates domain consistency and required fields.
Parses flexible environment specifications.
Supports permanent environment for network connectivity.
Extracts dependency configuration for retry logic.
Single responsibility: YAML → Task object conversion.
end note

note bottom of TaskInfo
**Enhanced Task Metadata**
Now includes three distinct pre-rendered prompts:
- instruction_prompt: Agent instructions
- assistant_prompt: Assistant context
- submit_prompt: Submission guidance
Replaces single "initial_prompt" field.
Includes max_steps for client-side step limit enforcement.
end note

@enduml
